  "id": "COMPOUND:22101 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide appears to interact with Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular pathways involving UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1A4. This enzyme is a target of Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide, and it, in turn, is targeted by a complex, structurally diverse compound that includes (17S)-9-hydroxy-4,5-dimethoxy-16-oxa-24-azapentacyclo[15.7.1.18,12.02,7.019,24]hexacosa-2,4,6,8,10,12(26)-hexaen-15-one, which also targets Neuropilin-2. The evidence suggests that Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide may influence Neuropilin-2 through a mechanism involving UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1A4, which is a key enzyme in the glucuronidation of various substrates. The presence of multiple, structurally distinct compounds that share the same target of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1A4 indicates that the interaction may be mediated through this enzyme, potentially modulating the activity of Neuropilin-2. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide to influence Neuropilin-2 through a complex, multi-step molecular mechanism involving glucuronidation and enzyme activity.",
